# Generated capability deck: a 3 MB self-contained HTML plus its rasters,
# rebuilt on demand from docs/presentations/generate/. Kept out of history.
docs/presentations/
.tmp_pytex_platform_deck/

# Local figure-inspection scratch pages
.fig_*.html

# Reference PDF corpus: a local working library, not a repository asset.
# PDFs are never tracked - cite them by DOI in references/reference_index.md
# instead. The eight that predated this rule were purged from history on
# 2026-08-09 (git filter-repo), removing ~107 MB; scripts/check_repo_integrity.py
# now rejects any tracked PDF with no exceptions.
references/*.pdf

# Kearns-parameter reference corpus: vendor PDFs plus several MB of raw XRDML
# instrument data, used as a local source for tutorial 31 and never a repository
# asset. Cite the papers by DOI in references/reference_index.md instead.
kearns_parameter_data_references/

# The workbench's live deployment configuration and its feedback store. The
# annotated template `config/pytex_app.example.yml` is tracked and is the file
# to read; the filled-in copy names an internal relay and may carry a local
# path, and the store is user-submitted content that belongs to the deployment
# rather than to the repository.
pytex_app.yml
feedback.json

# Everything above serves one cardinal rule, stated in AGENTS.md under
# "Repository content: sources and canonical assets only": if a command in this
# repository can regenerate a file, it is committed only when documentation, a
# test, a manifest, or a pinned baseline refers to it by name. Add the entry here
# before or in the commit that first produces the artifact - history is permanent,
# so a stray committed once is carried by every clone forever.

# The in-app documentation bundle: Sphinx output rendered into the package by
# `scripts/build_docs_bundle.py` immediately before a wheel is built. It is
# regenerable and large, so it is packaged rather than committed.
src/pytex/app/static/docs/
docs/_build/bundle-doctrees/
# myst-nb writes its executed notebooks beside the Sphinx output directory, so
# bundling into the package drops this alongside the docs. The bundle script
# removes it, and it is ignored so an interrupted build cannot leave it staged.
src/pytex/app/static/jupyter_execute/
